    },
    {
      "block": "library/9789240122925-eng/blocks/prose-sec-016",
      "source": "sections/sec-016-42-health-workforce-ageing-by-occupation.md",
      "source_hash": "d0e8f79ffeaecdd46d36e39bcb731a833cfedd66390e4530b0bd9c5f34b66d65",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Compares the age profiles of medical doctors and nursing personnel across income groups, showing that high-income countries face higher proportions of health workers aged 55 years and older while low- and lower-middle-income countries have predominantly younger workforces under age 35.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "conversation://e083ca61-5100-484e-9e88-6af4ce3f56a1"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-10-30"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/9789240122925-eng/blocks/prose-sec-017",
      "source": "sections/sec-017-43-health-workforce-gap-due-to-population-and-he.md",
      "source_hash": "8e8d65e642c402961a4f62dd3c2c83493194b60b76719ae66223ea947cebecff",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Projects the 2024–2030 health workforce gap arising from simultaneous population and workforce ageing, finding that 45 countries (including 17 in the WHO European Region) face declining workforce density by 2030 and estimating an additional need for 4.8 million health workers if age-specific utilization is accounted for.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "conversation://e083ca61-5100-484e-9e88-6af4ce3f56a1"
